  "description": "ELEBAZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C69 H115 Dy3 Mn4 N3 O28. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.977-3.936 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.31-132.54°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C69H115Dy3Mn4N3O28. Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III).",
